      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND STUDY AIMS",
          "content": "Double balloon enteroscopy (DBE) is a new technique for the visualization of the small bowel. Although the technique is widely used, little is known about the complications. A few complications have been reported in the literature, mainly in case reports. The aim of this study was to establish the complication rate of both diagnostic and therapeutic DBE."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS AND METHODS",
          "content": "A total of 10 centers (nine academic centers and one teaching hospital) across four continents participated in the study. Complications were defined according to the literature. A therapeutic DBE was defined as a DBE with use of argon plasma coagulation, a polypectomy snare, injection of fluids (other than ink for marking), removal of foreign body, or balloon dilation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "A total 85 adverse events were reported in 2362 DBE procedures. In all, 40 events fulfilled the definition of a complication, 13 in 1728 diagnostic DBE (0.8 %) and 27 during 634 therapeutic procedures (4.3 %). The complications were rated minor in 21 (0.9 %), moderate in 6 (0.3 %) and severe in 13 procedures (0.6 %). No fatal complications were reported. Seven cases of pancreatitis were reported, six after diagnostic (0.3 %) and one after therapeutic (0.2 %) DBE."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Diagnostic DBE is safe with a low complication rate. The complication rate of therapeutic DBE is high compared with therapeutic colonoscopy. The reason for this is unclear. The incidence of pancreatitis after DBE is low (0.3 %), but has to be considered in patients with persistent abdominal complaints after a DBE procedure."
        }
      ]},
